statement:
Let P, n ∈ ℕ, let U ⊆ ℝ^P be open, and let N ⊆ ℝ^P be an arbitrary set. Let T ∈ 𝒟_n(U) be minimizing in U ∩ N in the sense of Simon 7.1.1 (IsMinimizingIn): T is integer multiplicity, and M_W(T) ≤ M_W(S) for every open W ⊂⊂ U and every integer multiplicity S ∈ 𝒟_n(U) with ∂S = ∂T and spt(S − T) a compact subset of U ∩ N ∩ W. Assume spt T ⊆ N and ∂T = 0 in U, let R = (M, θ, ξ) represent T, and let μ_T = R.measure.
Let z₀ ∈ spt T and r > 0 with B_r(z₀) ⊆ U, and let N₀ ≥ 1 be an integer such that θ(x) = N₀ for μ_T-a.e. x ∈ B_r(z₀) and HasMassDensity T z₀ N₀ holds (Θ^n(μ_T, z₀) = N₀).
Then there is T₀ ∈ 𝒟_n(B_r(z₀)) (namely T₀ = N₀^{−1}·T restricted to B_r(z₀)) with the following properties:
- T₀ is minimizing in B_r(z₀) ∩ N;
- spt T₀ ⊆ N;
- ∂T₀ = 0 in B_r(z₀);
- M_W(T₀) < ∞ for every open W with W̄ compact ⊆ B_r(z₀);
- z₀ ∈ spt T₀;
- HasMassDensity T₀ z₀ 1;
- z₀ ∈ reg T₀ implies z₀ ∈ reg T.
